# CLI Reference

Complete reference for all Loom CLI commands.

## Global Options

| Option | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `--help, -h` | Show help message |
| `--version, -V` | Show version number |
| `--server-url` | Override server URL |
| `--verbose, -v` | Enable verbose output |

## Commands

### `loom`

Start a new interactive thread in the current workspace.

```bash
loom
```

### `loom list`

List recent threads.

```bash
loom list
```

### `loom resume`

Resume an existing thread. If no ID is provided, Loom resumes the most recent thread.

```bash
loom resume
loom resume <thread-id>
```

### `loom private`

Start a private local-only thread that never syncs to the server.

```bash
loom private
```

### `loom search`

Search threads by content, repository metadata, or commit SHA.

```bash
loom search "refactor auth flow"
```

### `loom share`

Update the visibility of a synced thread or share it with support.

```bash
loom share <thread-id> --visibility public
loom share <thread-id> --support
```

### `loom login`

Authenticate with the Loom server.

```bash
loom login [--provider <name>]
```

<Callout variant="info">
	Supported providers: `github`, `google`, `magic-link`
</Callout>

### `loom logout`

Clear authentication credentials.

```bash
loom logout
```

### `loom weaver`

Manage remote execution environments.

```bash
loom weaver ps             # List running weavers
loom weaver create         # Create a new weaver
loom weaver delete <id>    # Delete a weaver
```
